### 22. Definition of Done

The first release candidate is complete only when:

- Two Android phones can create independent identities.
- Users can exchange and verify public keys.
- Private keys are protected locally.
- A user can protect a contact or conversation with a password.
- Two devices can exchange authenticated, encrypted messages over a supported local transport without internet access.
- Intermediate relay devices cannot decrypt the end-to-end message.
- Multi-hop delivery works across a tested chain of devices.
- Duplicate packets and routing loops are controlled.
- Message status accurately reflects delivery.
- Bluetooth and microphone permissions are respected.
- The application builds reproducibly.
- Core automated tests pass.
- Known limitations are documented.

Real-time voice calls, high-density scaling, and continuous background operation must be reported as validated only after appropriate physical-device testing.

